    },
    {
      "id": "bote_b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -230,
      "y": 896,
      "width": 820.8,
      "height": 337.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "boundElements": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "aW",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "Users: 40M a month  (Padlet VP Growth, ClickHouse blog, Mar 2026)\nTeachers: 10% of users = 4M  (A)\nRun live lessons: 5% of teachers = 200k  (A)\nLessons: 3 a week, 40 min each  (A)  ->  2.6M a month = 1.7M lesson-hours\nPer school day (21 a month): 2.6M / 21 = 124k lessons\nBusiest hour: 12% of the day's lessons start  (A: US morning)  = 15k\nPeak live lessons: 15k x 0.67 h = ~10,000 at once\nAudio in at peak: 10k x 32 KB/s = 320 MB/s  (~2.6 Gbit/s)\nGPUs at peak: 10k / 100 per L4 (est.*) = 100, +30% spare = ~130 L4\nJev at peak: 6 settled sentences a min (A) x 10k = ~1,000 calls/s\nLLM at peak: Jev says draw on 15% (A) = ~150 calls/s\nStorage: ~150 KB of text per lesson = ~0.4 TB a month; audio: 0\n\n* H100 runs ~560 streams (NVIDIA, via MarkTechPost, Jan 2026); an L4 has\n  ~1/5 the power. Modal ran 127 streams on one GPU. Measure before trusting.",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1690733719,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "Users: 40M a month  (Padlet VP Growth, ClickHouse blog, Mar 2026)\nTeachers: 10% of users = 4M  (A)\nRun live lessons: 5% of teachers = 200k  (A)\nLessons: 3 a week, 40 min each  (A)  ->  2.6M a month = 1.7M lesson-hours\nPer school day (21 a month): 2.6M / 21 = 124k lessons\nBusiest hour: 12% of the day's lessons start  (A: US morning)  = 15k\nPeak live lessons: 15k x 0.67 h = ~10,000 at once\nAudio in at peak: 10k x 32 KB/s = 320 MB/s  (~2.6 Gbit/s)\nGPUs at peak: 10k / 100 per L4 (est.*) = 100, +30% spare = ~130 L4\nJev at peak: 6 settled sentences a min (A) x 10k = ~1,000 calls/s\nLLM at peak: Jev says draw on 15% (A) = ~150 calls/s\nStorage: ~150 KB of text per lesson = ~0.4 TB a month; audio: 0\n\n* H100 runs ~560 streams (NVIDIA, via MarkTechPost, Jan 2026); an L4 has\n  ~1/5 the power. Modal ran 127 streams on one GPU. Measure before trusting.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "updated": 1792580422027,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1970319818,
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
